data: {"runId":"run-a9633174-aac2-42a6-8c04-65e37d4fa600","status":"FINISHED","text":"Here is what each search returned. Nothing was modified, committed, pushed, or opened as a PR.\n\n**Semantic search (SSE decoding)**  \nSSE wire-format parsing lives in two in-repo places:\n\n1. **TypeScript SDK** — `createSseClient` in 12 generated copies of `packages/sdk/generated/*/core/serverSentEvents.gen.ts`. It reads `response.body` via `TextDecoderStream`, splits on `\\n\\n`, and parses `data:` / `event:` / `id:` / `retry:` lines. Wired from each service’s `client.gen.ts` via `makeSseFn`. No current product callers of `client.sse.*`.\n\n2. **Rust Anthropic client** — `Client::post_stream` in `crates/anthropic/src/client/mod.rs`. Line-oriented parse of `data: ` prefixes from the HTTP body; called from `Chat::create_stream`. JSON is then deserialized as `StreamEvent`.\n\nRelated but not in-repo: `eventsource-stream` inside `async-openai` / `rig-core`. Product chat streaming uses WebSocket JSON (`connection_gateway`), not HTTP SSE. There is no `SseDecoder` type.\n\n**Grep (`SseDecoder`)**  \nNo matches.\n\n**Glob (`*.sse`)**  \n0 files found.","durationMs":86973,"git":{"branches":[{"repoUrl":"github.com/macro-inc/macro","branch":"cursor/sse-decoding-investigation-1960"}]}}

